user_prompt:
Normalize and index two finalized claim-line sets so they can be reconciled deterministically downstream: the AI final output (ai_final_claim) and the Human final output (human_final_claim, post-validation). Produce a Normalized Reconciliation Package containing canonical line objects for AI and Human, stable keys for diffing, indexes for O(1) lookup, and parsing/serialization diagnostics.

Deterministic parsing rules (apply strictly):
- Each inbound line's cpt_code follows one of these formats: CODE, CODE*UNITS, CODE-MOD, CODE-MOD*UNITS, matching the regex ^[A-Z0-9]{4,5}(-[A-Z0-9]{1,3})?(\*[0-9]+)?$.
- Parse algorithm: (1) validate cpt_code against the regex; (2) split on '*' to extract units if present; (3) split the remaining part on '-' to extract modifier if present; (4) the remaining token is code_base.
- Units resolution precedence: if cpt_code includes *N, canonical units=N; else canonical units=inbound.units.
- Modifier resolution precedence: if cpt_code includes -MOD, canonical modifier=MOD; else canonical modifier=inbound.modifier.
- Rebuild display_code from (code_base, modifier, units): start with code_base; if modifier is non-empty append -<modifier>; if units > 1 append *<units>.
- If inbound cpt_code conflicts with inbound units or inbound modifier, prefer the parsed values from cpt_code for canonical fields and emit a parse_warnings[] entry describing the mismatch (warning_code MODIFIER_MISMATCH or UNITS_MISMATCH).
- Compute stable identity keys: line_key = <line_type>|<coding_system>|<code_base>|<modifier>. units are compared separately via units_key and are NOT part of line_key, so unit mismatches remain detectable downstream.
- If a line cannot be parsed cleanly, keep it in the normalized output with best-effort parsing and add a parse_warnings[] entry with warning_code=INVALID_FORMAT.
- Validation: every normalized line must have a non-empty line_key and code_base, units must be an integer >= 1, and display_code must equal its rebuilt serialization.
- Parse human_final_claim raw code lines (one code per line) into result line objects using: cpt_code = the raw line string; coding_system = CPT_II if it matches ^[0-9]{4}[A-Z]$, HCPCS if it starts with a letter (e.g., G, J, A), otherwise CPT_I; line_type = QUALITY if coding_system is CPT_II, otherwise BILLABLE; units parsed from *N (default 1); modifier parsed from -MOD (default "").

Do not add or remove lines, change clinical interpretation, apply payer/specialty rules, or score/adjudicate anything.

Return ONLY this JSON object (no markdown, no extra text):
{
  "recon_normalized_package": {
    "document_id": "doc_...",
    "human_submission_context": {
      "is_post_validation": true,
      "validated_by": "",
      "validation_standard": "",
      "validation_timestamp": "",
      "notes": ""
    },
    "normalized_ai_lines": [
      {
        "source": "AI",
        "line_key": "",
        "coding_system": "CPT_I|CPT_II|HCPCS",
        "line_type": "BILLABLE|QUALITY",
        "code_base": "",
        "modifier": "",
        "units": 1,
        "display_code": "",
        "raw": {
          "cpt_code": "",
          "units": 1,
          "modifier": ""
        }
      }
    ],
    "normalized_human_lines": [
      {
        "source": "HUMAN",
        "line_key": "",
        "coding_system": "CPT_I|CPT_II|HCPCS",
        "line_type": "BILLABLE|QUALITY",
        "code_base": "",
        "modifier": "",
        "units": 1,
        "display_code": "",
        "raw": {
          "cpt_code": "",
          "units": 1,
          "modifier": ""
        }
      }
    ],
    "indexes": {
      "ai_by_line_key": {
        "<line_key>": [
          "idx0",
          "idx1"
        ]
      },
      "human_by_line_key": {
        "<line_key>": [
          "idx0",
          "idx1"
        ]
      }
    },
    "parse_warnings": [
      {
        "warning_code": "INVALID_FORMAT|MODIFIER_MISMATCH|UNITS_MISMATCH|MISSING_FIELDS",
        "message": "",
        "source": "AI|HUMAN",
